# Title: PowerShell Download Pattern
# ID: 3b6ab547-8ec2-4991-b9d2-2b06702a48d7
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), oscd.community, Jonhnathan Ribeiro
# Date: 2019-01-16
# Tags: attack.execution, attack.t1059.001
# Description: Detects a Powershell process that contains download commands in its command line string
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog (((process_exec="*new-object*" AND process_exec="*net.webclient).*" AND process_exec="*download*") AND (process_exec="*string(*" OR process_exec="*file(*")) AND (((process_path="*\\powershell_ise.exe" OR process_path="*\\powershell.exe" OR process_path="*\\pwsh.exe")) OR ((process_name="PowerShell_ISE.EXE" OR process_name="PowerShell.EXE" OR process_name="pwsh.dll"))))
